---
3md: 1.0
view: blend
category: Creative
axis: base
legend: .=· #=●
billboard: true
title: DNA Double Helix - depth is the strand
molecule: B-form DNA (idealized)
pairs: "20"
twist: 36 degrees per base pair
render: blend the rungs to fuse them into a twisting double helix you can orbit; play to climb the strand base by base
---
A double helix where the molecule's length is the Z axis. Each plane is one
base-pair rung. A dot is an empty cell, a hash is the sugar-phosphate backbone,
and the two letters are the base pair. The backbones turn 36 degrees per step.
Blending all 20 rungs stacks the spiral. Climb from [[z=0|the first pair]] to
[[z=19|the last]].

